{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Which bills land in which pay period, and on what due date. Two kinds of case. kind 'periods': input { kind, anchor: date, now: local date-time, bills: [Bill] } (Bill shape and defaults in README.md). The three periods come from the pay-periods rules; expected { periods: [ { label, key, start, end, bills: [ { id, dueDate } ] } ] }. Rules by bill.rate (case-sensitive): 'Monthly' is due on the first of (previous, same, next) month relative to the period's start month whose due date falls inside [start, end]; a due date is month-start + (dueDay - 1) days, so a day past the month's end overflows into the next month (31 in April is May 1, 29/30/31 in Feb 2025 are Mar 1/2/3) and is never clamped. 'Bi-Weekly' is in every period with dueDate = period start, whatever dueDay says. 'Yearly' uses yearlyDate 'MM-DD' in the period start's year, then the next year, with the same overflow (02-29 in 2025 is Mar 1); a yearlyDate that does not split into exactly two integers, or whose month is outside 1..12, never lands. 'Once' and any other rate never land. Inactive bills never land. Within a period bills are ordered by dueDate ascending; equal dates keep input order. kind 'monthlyDueDate': input { kind, dueDay, periodStart, periodEnd } -> expected { dueDate: date or null }, the Monthly rule on its own for an arbitrary window (first match in the order previous, same, next month).",
